  "summary": "All 8 results-inbox items are worked and closed per RBC-INBOX-01. For each, the patient was confirmed by two identifiers.\n\n1. task-00001, Raj Patel, positive FIT: an active GI colonoscopy referral already existed (sr-00001), so I linked it and placed no duplicate (RBC-GI-01 §2). Patient messaged; note written.\n2. task-00002, Leslie Parisian, renal ultrasound: simple 1.8 cm right renal cyst; the radiologist recommends no follow-up imaging. Closed with a comment that no follow-up is needed (RBC-INBOX-01 §3).\n3. task-00006 and task-00007, Edra Ondricka: TSH and lipid panel are normal. Acknowledged and closed.\n4. task-00005, Linda Marsh, outside ED CT abdomen/pelvis from 2026-06-04: the 5 mm right lower lobe nodule is already followed in lung cancer screening (LDCT 2025-09-15, Lung-RADS 2). Her annual screening CT was due 9/15, and the ±1-month window has passed. Per RBC-RAD-05 §2 I ordered the screening CT within 14 days (sr-t0007, window 10/23 to 11/06) with a tracking task due 11/06 (task-t0008). Patient messaged; note written. The 3 mm kidney stone from the ED visit should be reviewed at her next visit.\n5. task-00014, Tomás Ruiz (16), knee X-ray: aggressive lytic lesion of the distal right femur, suspected primary bone tumour. Ordered an urgent orthopaedic oncology referral (sr-t0012) and urgent MRI of the femur with and without contrast (sr-t0013), both by 11/05 (RBC-RAD-05 §3). Tracking tasks are due 11/05. I chose a phone call to his mother rather than a portal message and assigned it for today to J. Reyes, NP, who ordered the X-ray (task-t0014). Note written.\n6. task-00004, Denise Holloway: potassium 6.2, not hemolyzed. Creatinine is 1.58 and she started lisinopril on 10/06. On-call was messaged at stat priority with a call task (task-t0023), and a stat repeat BMP is ordered (sr-t0019). Patient messaged today; note written. I suggested on-call consider holding lisinopril; I did not change her medications myself.\n7. task-00003, Walter Brenna